# Story 50: Editing Files (50s)
# Hook: When the agent edits a file, you see the diff first -- every write waits for your yes.
# Duration: 50s
# Source: story-050-editing-files.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 7

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
When the agent edits a file, you see the diff first -- every write waits for your yes.

[00:03.0 --> 00:08.0]
Launch rysh and drop in a small file we can have the agent edit.

[00:08.0 --> 00:14.0]
In shell mode, create a quick README so there's something to change.

[00:14.0 --> 00:20.0]
Double-press Escape to enter prompt mode.

[00:20.0 --> 00:36.0]
Ask it to change a line. The agent uses file_edit for an exact-string replace, multi_edit for several atomic hunks, file_write to create files, or apply_patch for a unified diff. Each of these is approval-gated.

[00:36.0 --> 00:45.0]
The footer shows the action with a diff preview. Press y to approve, capital Y to approve always, n to reject, or capital N to reject with a reason.

[00:45.0 --> 00:50.0]
Nothing touches your files until you approve the diff.

